menu "Stadiacast dongle"

config DONGLE_SSID
    string "Hotspot SSID"
    default "stadiacast-dongle"
    help
        Network the Stadia controller joins. Provision the controller with this name
        (stadiacast-provision) and use the same name and password for the PC hotspot,
        so the controller works with either.

config DONGLE_PASSWORD
    string "Hotspot password (WPA2, 8 to 63 characters)"
    default "stadiacast"

config DONGLE_CHANNEL
    int "Wi-Fi channel"
    range 1 13
    default 6

config DONGLE_USB_AUDIO
    bool "USB headphones for the controller's headset jack"
    default y
    help
        Besides the gamepad, the board shows up as USB headphones (48 kHz stereo). What the
        computer plays there goes to the controller's 3.5 mm jack as Opus. Turn it off to be a
        gamepad only, as in step 3.

config DONGLE_OPUS_COMPLEXITY
    int "Opus encoder complexity"
    range 1 10
    default 8
    depends on DONGLE_USB_AUDIO
    help
        Higher is better sound for more CPU time per 20 ms frame. The serial log prints the
        encode time every 10 s while audio plays.

endmenu
